    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d781">

                <pb facs="0905" n="893" xml:id="pg893"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811B.001 Quezon, Manuel L./165</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Adviser on Political Relations</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hornbeck</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Chief of Staff</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Marshall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-02-02">February 2, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reference, your memorandum for Mr. Hornbeck and Mr. Hamilton of February 2 and
                    its enclosure.</p>
                <p>It occurs to Mr. Hamilton and me to ask: Ought not this matter now be taken up
                    again with the President?</p>
                <p>Presumably the question of making plans and issuing instructions would lie with
                    you and Admiral King.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d781-f1"/></p>
                <p>Mr. Hamilton and I are at your service and would be glad to come to you for
                    conference should you so desire or to collaborate with you in any manner which
                    may be helpful to you.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d781-f1" n="32" xml:id="d781-f1-content">
                <p>Adm. Ernest J. King, Commander in Chief of the U. S. Fleet.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
